From cdf6054ef35fcd8b045838af69c67c3d736278d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilyriehl <eriehl@jhu.edu>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:06:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Relay: close the previous level's document before opening
 the next one

All levels map to the same server-side file. When the client opens the next level without closing the previous document, the old file worker keeps serving the previous level's environment and every Game.getProofState for the new level fails with "Level not found" (server trace "no world id"). The relay now sends a didClose for the previous document itself. Also logs which level each proof-state request targets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
