From 459c12673f070326a77658d14566d57727a41124 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilyriehl <eriehl@jhu.edu>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:15:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] One virtual folder for all level documents

vscode-lean4 keeps one Lean client per folder, so naming levels file:///<world>/<level>.lean made the client open a second server connection on a world change while the infoview kept using the first; every proof-state request for the new level then failed with "Level not found" until a page reload. Levels are now file:///levels/<world>__<level>.lean; the relay parses that and maps server messages back to it.

